---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Link from '../components/Link';

import {
  author,
  jobTitle,
  socialLinks,
  cleanJobTitle
} from '../config/site.ts';

import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import meImage from '../assets/me.jpg';

const title = "About | " + author + " - " + jobTitle;
const description = "Learn about " + author + "'s approach to building joint ecosystems of hardware and software. Discover his principles of shared understanding, structural integrity, and architectural clarity.";
const keywords = author + ", engineering philosophy, systems architecture, hardware-software bridge, shared understanding, 0-to-1 phase, software engineering rigor, tech leadership";
const localImage = "/og/about.png";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  keywords={keywords}
  localImage={localImage}
>
  <section class="flex-card">

    <!-- Profile Photo -->
    <div class="profile-image-floater">
        <Image
          src={meImage}
          alt="Portrait of {author}"
          width={160}
          height={160}
          loading="eager"
        />
    </div>

    <!-- Text Content -->
    <div>
      <h1>About Me</h1>

      <p>
        I am a <strong><span class="whitespace-nowrap">{cleanJobTitle}</span></strong> specializing in the intersection of hardware and software. My work is driven by a core conviction: the most impactful technology emerges when we treat silicon and code as a <strong>unified ecosystem</strong>, not as separate domains.
      </p>

      <h2>The Journey to the "Bridge"</h2>

      <p>
        My fascination with systems began with a computer and no internet — a constraint that forced me to understand how software interacts with hardware at the most fundamental level. That early curiosity evolved into a career centered on <strong>Hardware-Software Co-Design</strong>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Today, I develop system-level solutions and the infrastructure — such as <strong>compilers, simulators, and embedded firmware</strong> — that eliminate inefficiencies between disciplines. By applying software engineering rigor to co-design, I help establish the <strong>Hardware-Software Bridge</strong>, enabling a <strong>joint ecosystem</strong> where silicon architecture and system software evolve in harmony. This ensures that the final systems are not only high-performance but also sustainable, built on a foundation of <em>shared clarity and purpose</em>.
      </p>

      <h2>Where I Thrive: The "0 to 1" Phase</h2>

      <p>
        I am at my best in the <strong>design and innovation phases</strong>, where the solution space is open and the architecture is yet to be defined. I find deep fulfillment in "0 to 1" projects, where I can:
        <ul>
          <li>Establish a holistic system architecture from the ground up.</li>
          <li>Build the tooling and CI pipelines that enable rapid, reliable iteration.</li>
          <li>Transform hardware constraints into opportunities for elegant, purposeful software design.</li>
        </ul>
      </p>

      <h2>Engineering with Purpose</h2>

      <p>
        At my core, I believe good engineering is about more than technical excellence — it is about <strong>shared understanding</strong>. Its true value is unlocked when a team moves forward with clarity, purpose, and alignment.
      </p>

      <p>
        I work pragmatically, navigating real-world trade-offs while staying true to broader goals. Whether I am architecting an API or aligning a cross-functional team, I prioritize <strong>logical clarity, reliability, and developer empowerment</strong> — ensuring the systems we build are resilient, purposeful, and easy for others to build upon.
      </p>

      <h2>Beyond the Code</h2>

      <p>
        Outside of engineering, I explore the human side of technology. I am fascinated by psychology, communication dynamics, and the art of distilling complex topics into simple, actionable insights. These interests directly shape my leadership style and my approach to remote-first collaboration.
      </p>

      <p>
        I share my evolving thoughts on engineering efficiency, leadership, and systems-level thinking on my <Link href="/blog">blog</Link>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="muted-top-rule">Next Steps</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Technical Context:</strong> Explore my <Link href="/portfolio">project portfolio</Link></li>
        <li><strong>Professional Background:</strong> <Link href="/resume" download>Download my Résumé (PDF)</Link> or <Link href="/resume-overview">view details online</Link></li>
        <li><strong>Let's Connect:</strong> I am always open to discussing complex system architectures, hardware acceleration, RISC-V, or remote-first collaborations. Reach out via <Link href={socialLinks.email}>email</Link> or <Link href={socialLinks.linkedin}>LinkedIn</Link>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
